A:

In your program, m is a local variable and has a scope of function main(), therefore it will not be available anywhere else in your program. If you want it to be available outside the function, declare it as global variable.
Either change it to int m[100]={1,2,3}; or declare it as global like this
int m[3]={1,2,3};

For #1 to work, you should declare int m[100]={1,2,3}; outside the function first.
